  "slug": "gene-rna-d705",
  "summary": "Recent preprints extend RNA fate, nascent transcript localization, LTR chromatin and Argonaute network analyses across model systems.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is how RNA processing, spatial organization and chromatin engagement determine gene expression output. A full-length capped RNA study in mouse embryonic stem cells connects exosome surveillance of PROMPTs and transcript architecture to RNA fate and regulatory state. In Drosophila spermatocytes, nascent kl-3 transcripts show spatial segregation of exonic and intronic RNA on the Y-loop, with Smooth protein required for this organization. In mouse and human pluripotent stem cells, SMARCA4 preferentially occupies lineage-specific LTR retrotransposons co-bound by POU5F1 and SOX2, linking repeat elements to chromatin regulatory architecture. Argonomics Explorer provides a searchable resource for comparing Argonaute-sRNA and AGO-target interactions across public small RNA datasets. What is new is the resolution of transcript architecture and spatial RNA localization at the level of individual loci, together with repeat-element engagement by pluripotency factors.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
